# Success Criteria

The model succeeds when:

CAS correctly identifies the demands of each combat sport.

Programming reflects those demands.

Transfer to competition improves.

Recommendations remain individualized.

Scientific consistency is maintained.

---

# Final Principle

Every combat sport is different.

Every athlete is different.

The principles of human performance remain the same.

CAS understands the universal principles first,

then specializes them for each discipline.